search-shaping -- a wall-clock budget on the search (gh-ocannl-1409): it decides how many candidates are attempted before the search crowns its incumbent, never what a crowned schedule means or how fast it runs. The crown of a search it cut is stored marked as cut (Schedule_cache.entry's budget_cut), so only a call that also has a budget replays it -- an incomplete measurement set must not become every later call's answer, the rule that keeps a contended search out of the cache
  autotune_budget_seconds

keyed: timing -- it picks the OBJECTIVE a candidate is timed against -- the latency of a lone dispatch, or what the kernel sustains under queue depth -- and the two crown different candidates, measured (gh-ocannl-755). Not Search_shaping, which is where it started and where the neighbouring autotune_* knobs correctly sit: those change how carefully the SAME quantity is measured, so either process's winner answers the other's question, whereas an entry crowned under isolated timing is the answer to a question a queued search did not ask -- and its stored best_ms, baseline_ms and mma_best_ms are readings of a different quantity, which a replay copies into the reading process's report under that process's label. Left unkeyed, a warm cache would also defeat the new default outright, replaying isolated-crowned winners forever (Codex P1 on PR #512)
  autotune_timing [read at codegen]

placement-shaping -- it makes the tuner try alternative inlining decisions; each alternative is a different program and keys on its own digest
  tune_flip_ordering
  tune_flip_profit_margin
  tune_inline_flips

placement-shaping -- a wall-clock budget on the whole Train.tune_placements call (gh-ocannl-1440), split among its searches: no Autotune.tune reads the key -- a search receives only its share (Autotune.call_budget), which cuts it by autotune_budget_seconds' rule and marks a cut crown budget_cut, so only a budgeted call replays it. Out of the trajectory identity because the share changes with the wall clock, and a cut trajectory is a prefix of the same candidate order, which early stopping reads conservatively (a slower incumbent abandons fewer flips)
  tune_call_budget_seconds

placement-shaping -- it decides which of the two searched placement arms ships, overriding the measured comparison rather than changing either arm: each arm is a different program keyed on its own digest, each arm's crown is cached under that digest either way, and a schedule crowned under one setting is a valid crown under the other (gh-ocannl-638)
  tune_ship_arm

placement-shaping -- it decides whether the placement decision is replayed from the placement-decision store or re-derived by comparing the two arms (gh-ocannl-1020): each arm and each flip is a different program keyed on its own digest and cached either way, the store holds only which of them shipped, and a decision re-derived from the arms is as valid a winner as a replayed one
  tune_placement_store

untimed-model -- it steers Autotune.model_default -- whether the recipes' untuned compiles route through it, how many placement levels it branch-and-bounds, whether its family search lifts the tile-size lattice -- which picks by the analytic model without timing anything and never reads or writes the schedule cache; Autotune.tune reads none of them. The envelope keys (model_peak_flops, model_peak_memory_bandwidth) stay search-shaping: tune's keep-fraction ranking and bound pruning read them too
  model_default_geometry_lattice
  model_default_placements
  model_default_schedule

untimed-model -- they are the cache capacity, cache bandwidth, scalar issue rate, DRAM rate, tile-MMA rate, device-gather rate and launch-fill constants of the analytic model's ranking score (gh-ocannl-1253, gh-ocannl-1442, gh-ocannl-1479, gh-ocannl-1495), which only the untimed choosers read (Autotune.model_default's pick, and the auto seeding gate of Autotune.seeded_default) -- like the backends' advisory cache_capacity_bytes, cache_bandwidth, issue_rate, dram_bandwidth, mma_rate, device_gather_rate, multiprocessors and fill_threads they override, Untimed fields of the device description and outside the cache key for the same reason: a stored winner is a measured schedule, which they change neither the compilation nor the speed of. Autotune.tune's bound pruning and keep-fraction ranking read the distinct-cell roofline; the search reaches them only through the seeded plan it seeds first, which joins the trajectory identity as its content digest and, for a staffed start, as a gate tag naming these readings
  model_cache_bandwidth
  model_cache_capacity
  model_device_gather_rate
  model_dram_bandwidth
  model_fill_threads
  model_issue_rate
  model_mma_rate
  model_multiprocessors

